# Line endings are a cross-platform correctness problem here, not a preference.
# A shell script checked out with CRLF fails on Linux and macOS with
# "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env sh^M", so everything the repository executes is
# stored and checked out with LF. Only the Windows batch launchers need CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

switch text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf

*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.pfx binary
